# The fixed re-read: after the byte store, rep #$20 restores 16-bit BEFORE
# the address reload (lda N,s; tax), then sep #$20 for the byte load.
# Re-pinned 2026-07-22 (issue #132): the invariant is that the byte
# store's 8-bit mode is restored before ANY 16-bit address work, not the
# exact sequence that followed it. The emitter now recomputes the
# address (lda/clc/adc) instead of reloading it, so the old regex no
# longer matched while the property it protects still held.
present sta\.l \$0000,x\n\trep #\$20
# The bug signature must never come back: byte store, then address reload
# + tax + byte load with NO mode switch between them — the store's 8-bit
# mode leaked through, so the reload ran in 8-bit and grabbed only the low
# byte. (Verified this exact regex matched the pre-fix output.)
absent sta\.l \$0000,x\n\tlda \d+,s\n\ttax\n\tlda\.l \$0000,x
